course: dictionary
lesson: 175
title: Agree and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word agree can mean several things, and the context tells you which one. «I agree with you» means you have the same opinion as someone. «She agreed to help» means she said yes.
explain: «We agreed on a plan» means we decided something together. «The two answers agree» means the numbers match, so both are right. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Agree can also be about food. «The cheese doesn't agree with me» means it makes my tummy feel bad, so it does not suit me.
fact: Agree is a verb: agree, agrees, agreed, agreeing.
fact: «Would they agree to it?» asks if people will say yes to an idea.
fact: «The two answers agree» means the answers match.
fact: In grammar, a verb agrees with its subject: he runs, they run.
fact: The prime meridian through Greenwich in London was «agreed at a conference in Washington in 1884».
exercise: «I agree with you, Mum, that homework is hard.» What does agree mean here? | *Have the same opinion as someone | Say a loud no | Cook a tasty meal | Run very fast
exercise: «The two answers agree, so our maths must be right.» What does agree mean? | Argue | *Match | Forget | Disappear
exercise: «We agreed on a plan for the school trip.» What does agreed mean here? | Lost | *Decided together | Shouted | Forgot
test: «She agreed to help us clean the classroom.» What does agreed to help mean? | *Said yes to helping | Forgot to help | Refused to help
test: Which word completes the sentence: «They ___ to the plan.»? | agreed | agrees | agreeing | *agree
exam: Which sentence uses agree to mean the food suits you? | We agreed on a plan. | Two answers agree. | *The milk doesn't agree with me. | She agreed to come.
